{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511212-whereabouts-of-chantries-listed-in-the-book-of-chantries","id":1511212,"title":"Whereabouts of chantries listed in The Book of Chantries?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-10T05:01:48-07:00","id":1511212,"title":"Whereabouts of chantries listed in The Book of Chantries?","content":"The Book of Chantries is one of the first MtA books, even discussing Technocrats before the real Convention books released (of course a lot of out-of-date stuff). It does provide Chantry Creation rules, but more important is, introducing important chantries of the game. So I wonder the whereabouts of them? <br /> <br /> AFAIK:<br /> <br /> Doissetep (Destroyed by Technocracy, we all know)<br /> House of Helekar (We all also know, messed up by Voormas)<br /> The Lodge of the Gray Squirrel (Unknown, maybe lost in Avatar Storm)<br /> Vali Shallar (As above)<br /> The Sepulcher (Unknown, but may still alive because of its young)<br /> <br /> MECHA (Unknown, maybe lost in Avatar Storm)<br /> Null-B (Destroyed by Marauders in Guide to Technocracy)<br /> Research Plantation #4 (Unknown, but maybe destroyed by Verbena and hybrids, as stuff hints)<br /> <br /> Dracus Vachor (Unknown, maybe lost in Avatar Storm)<br /> The Houshold of the Jade Demon (As above, but some Revised stuff I read thinks it still exists)<br /> <br /> The Crombey Farm Chantry (Unknown, maybe simply fell due to Samuel Haight)<br /> <br /> Appendix One:<br /> <br /> Manse of Madness (Abandoned Chantry) (Unknown, maybe lost in Avatar Storm)<br /> The Flying Dutchman (As above)<br /> The Knights of Newark (Unknown)<br /> <br /> Balador (Lost in Avatar Storm)<br /> The Celestial Temple of the Sun (As above, in Revised Tradition book)<br /> The Nightmare Theatre (Unknown, but maybe destroyed by vampires, as stuff hints)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-10T15:26:20-07:00","id":1511291,"title":"","content":"The Sepulcher was a haunted house in Chicago, so it's probably still as is, baring potential changes in membership and who is in charge. If you wanted to incorporate the events of the Great Maelstrom and Hunter: The Reckoning in your game world, then it might've had an impact on the ghosts dwelling there and their situation, but that's up to you. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-11T14:32:44-07:00","id":1511408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1511212-whereabouts-of-chantries-listed-in-the-book-of-chantries#post1511212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Book of Chantries is one of the first MtA books, even discussing Technocrats before the real Convention books released (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider that it is important that Technocrats and their Faction, Conveitons, and Methodologies were mentioned, developed, detailed, and described since the 1st edition M:tA Corebooks and other literature like Player's Guides.<br /> Defeinitely and clearly there are many paragraphs written exclusively or mainly about the Technomancers and their thinking, capabilities attitude, and other qualities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}